# Pairs with RStrictIsolation. The receiver records every terminal of a saga it
# has not yet decided as a commit, whatever outcome it carries, so an aborted
# saga's tally completes as committed and its staged buckets surface post-saga
# on the receiver - a saga the origin aborted, made visible. A saga the receiver
# has already decided (a bootstrap's decision row) keeps its recorded outcome,
# so a re-shipped terminal is not refused as conflicting, which would leave it
# undeliverable and race the target against a deadlock.
MODULE: RStrictIsolationTerminalOutcomeIgnored
TARGET: RStrictIsolation
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the receiver records an undecided saga's terminals as a commit, so an aborted saga surfaces
PERTURBS: DeliverTerminal

--- FIND
           o == Outcome(m.commit)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the terminal's outcome is ignored; an undecided saga is recorded
\* as committed, and a decided one keeps its recorded outcome.
           o == IF rdec[TreeOf(m.key)] = "inflight" THEN "committed" ELSE rdec[TreeOf(m.key)]
--- END
